                                                "sense_id": "be87a6fc-3a05-30af-9f74-b20bae6b3d51",
                                                "text": "Slime moulds on Earth were a common research subject. Scientists had studied them for centuries because of their self-organizing capability, that enabled a loose mass of individual cells to act as a macro-organism, a predator even, all without any neurology whatsoever."
